Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(storage): make expired name reclaim generation-safe

Context:
Source review of PR #99 found that identical-body reclaim can admit two winners because Miniflare/R2 body-hash ETags do not change across metadata-only overwrites, and that expired legacy R2 objects without custom expiration metadata were no longer immediately reusable. Greptile also reported that a KV metadata put failure after a successful R2 claim stranded the name until expiry.

Expected behavior:
Expired-name reclaim still has exactly one winner when replacement bytes are identical. Legacy R2 objects without custom expiration metadata follow the existing KV expiration lookup. If KV indexing fails after this request won the R2 claim, the request fails and the incomplete claim is released so a retry can succeed without overwriting another winner.

Acceptance criteria:
- synchronized identical-body expired reclaim returns exactly one non-null claim
- expired legacy R2 names without custom metadata are reusable immediately
- KV metadata failure after a new named R2 claim leaves the name retryable
- existing distinct-body race and sequential 409 tests remain green

Constraints:
- generic upstream behavior only; no Feishu concepts
- no Durable Object, reservation namespace, or MPU redesign
- do not modify upstream-sync

Validation:
- RED: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts -> 3 failed (identical-body two winners, legacy null, retry 409)
- GREEN: same command -> 5 passed
- REFACTOR: prettier --check and eslint on changed files passed
- REGRESSION: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --project Workers -> 17 files, 119 tests passed
- tsc --noEmit passed

